Package: mos-podman
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: mos build <mos@example.invalid>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: mos-system, nftables, libsystemd0, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: mos container engine
 The seven binaries os/pkgs/podman compiles from pinned upstream source --
 podman and quadlet from containers/podman v5.8.6, crun 1.29.1, conmon v2.2.1,
 netavark v2.1.0, aardvark-dns v2.1.0 and catatonit v0.2.1 -- with the Quadlet
 system generator symlink, the /etc/containers configuration podman actually
 reads, and the Quadlet unit directory the operator writes into.
 .
 The versions are this repository's decision and not the distribution's: trixie
 ships podman 5.4.2, crun 1.21 and netavark 1.14, and os/pkgs/podman/versions.env
 is the upgrade interface for all six.
 .
 THE ENGINE SHIPS INSTALLED AND INERT. This payload carries no
 multi-user.target.wants symlink, because podman ships no service units at all:
 upstream's live in contrib/ and are installed by `make install.systemd`, which
 os/pkgs/podman does not run. The one unit here,
 etc-containers-systemd.mount, is installed and deliberately not enabled --
 statically enabling the bind would give anything able to write
 /mnt/state/quadlet a root-capable container at the next reboot with no operator
 decision in the path. mosd's ContainerReconciler enables and starts it from the
 container.enabled setting, which is the runtime-scoped enablement every other
 mos-driven unit uses.
 .
 THE THREE DEPENDENCIES BELOW ARE WRITTEN OUT BECAUSE dpkg-shlibdeps CANNOT SEE
 THEM. Everything it can see -- libjson-c5 for crun, libsubid5 and libseccomp2
 for podman, libcap2 for crun, libglib2.0-0t64 for conmon -- comes from
 ${shlibs:Depends} over the payload's ELF and is not restated here.
 .
 nftables is reached by exec, not by linking. netavark 2.1.0 has three firewall
 drivers (Firewalld, Nftables, Fwnone); the iptables driver was removed in 2.x,
 nftables is the compile-time default, and netavark runs `nft` off PATH. Without
 it the first `podman run` fails with "netavark: nftables error: unable to
 execute nft", and no NEEDED-soname check can predict that.
 .
 libsystemd0 is reached by dlopen, not by linking. go-systemd's sdjournal opens
 "libsystemd.so.0" by name at runtime, so podman's NEEDED entries do not mention
 it and ldd cannot find it; containers.conf sets log_driver = "journald", so the
 library's absence would lose container logs rather than fail loudly.
 libsystemd0 is the trixie package shipping that soname.
 .
 mos-system is depended on UNVERSIONED and deliberately so. It owns the mounts
 this package's configuration names: storage.conf puts the container graphroot
 on /srv/containers/storage, which is the DATA partition mos-system's fstab
 mounts, and etc-containers-systemd.mount binds /mnt/state/quadlet, which needs
 mos-seed-state.service from the same package. Nothing here is pinned to a
 mos-system built from this commit, so an exact-version dependency would assert
 a coupling that does not exist.
 .
 There is no dependency on mosd, mos-apid, mos-mqttd or mos-mqtt-broker. The
 engine is installed alongside them, not above them: it runs without any of them
 present, and mosd's use of it is mosd's dependency and not this one's.
